spec:
  grid: 9-30 rows x 8-20 cols, black background
  markers:
    yellow: 1-3 pixels, these are the square centers
    grey: 1-10 pixels, these are blockers that limit square size
  colors_present: exactly yellow and grey on black background (input); adds red (output)
  transform:
    - for each yellow pixel, find min Chebyshev distance D to any grey pixel
    - fill a (2*(D-1)+1)-square centered on yellow with red, only replacing black pixels
    - radius = D-1, range 1-5; the red square is the largest that stops one cell short of every grey blocker
  constraints:
    - radius >= 1 for every yellow marker (so min Chebyshev dist to any grey >= 2)
    - red square must fit entirely within grid (no clipping)
    - red squares of different yellow markers must not overlap [observed]
    - yellow and grey pixels are preserved in output (red only replaces black)

